Z||000003||JohnF||12-05-2001||05:19 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by carpetviper:<BR><B>If your looking for the 2M4, 2M6, and such then you might want to check out <A HREF="http://www.fierostore.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierostore.com</A> <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm familiar with FS.  I don't know of any engines beside the 4 or 6 you mention (didn't know the Fiero came in "and such")and I haven't a clue where to look in the FS catalog.  Any hints you could givewould be appreciated.<P>BTW - I went to a Pontiac dealer today.  Their statement was "We have only been here a year and don't know anything about the decals or stickers."<P>Odd, I thought the Emissions sticker was mandated by EPA requirements.  Wouldn't a body shop have to reinsall any mandated decals if removed?<P>Where would they get theirs?||||reg||9
Z||000004||jelly2m8||12-05-2001||06:14 PM||||2 years ago I purchased a new Emissions label ( sticker ) for my 87 2.8.<P> The dealer ship looked up the part number.<P>If they can't, post the year and engine thats in your car. I know my new emissions label has the part number on it, maybe someone can check theirs out.<P> Speaking of this, If someone can check their emissions label for a part number on a 88 V6 car, I'd appreciate it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||JohnF||12-05-2001||07:53 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR>[BThe dealer ship looked up the part number.<BR>...post the year and engine thats in your car. I know my new emissions label has the part number on it, maybe someone can check theirs out. <BR>[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>O.K.  I'm needing the P/N for the emissions sticker for an '88 Tech 4.  <P>I'm also needing the sticker P/N that, I think, stated to check owner's manual for coolant flushing procedures (at least, my '85GT has one) and I need the 88-C-23 recall sticker P/N that was applied by the checking Pontiac dealer after the recall inspection and changes.<P>Anything else?<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||T-top Fiero||12-05-2001||07:54 PM||||I looked up the part numbers for the '88 emission stickers (both 4 & 6 cylinders)in my 22P and then checked on gmpartsdirect web page to see if they were still available. Both came back as not available anymore.<BR>So unless someone out there makes a reproduction sticker you are both out of luck.||||reg||1
Z||000007||jelly2m8||12-05-2001||09:39 PM||||Thanks for the update T-top fiero. <BR>Well poo, guess a new one is out of the question.<P>JohnF,<P> I do have a 88 4 cyl, I'll get the number off of it, just fer kicks if you want it. If you know a good way of getting the sticker off without destroying it, lemme know, you can have mine.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||rockcrawl||12-05-2001||10:01 PM||||The GMpartsdirect part number search doesn't always come up with a part, even if the part is still available. I'd check with a local dealer. The recall decal (aluminum plate) is # 10167524||||reg||1
Z||000009||JohnF||12-06-2001||07:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B><BR> I do have a 88 4 cyl, I'll get the number off of it, just fer kicks if you want it. <BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'll take the number please.  I'll take the sticker, if you can get it!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||7
Z||000010||jelly2m8||12-06-2001||10:55 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JohnF:<BR><B> I'll take the number please.  I'll take the sticker, if you can get it!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>These are off of my 88 2.5L<P>Emissions label      10055656<BR>Coolant fill label   10060907<BR>Belt routing label   10044329<P> It's worth a shot to take these numbers to your dealer, and ask them to check them for a number change. If they come back as discontinued, which they probably will, ask them to do a search for them. The dealerships can check stock at other dealerships, and warehouses.<BR>  Even after a part is discontinued, you sometimes can find some old stock laying around. They just have to make the effort.<P>hope this helps,<P> I'll try and get those labels off without destroying them.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000011||JohnF||12-06-2001||12:00 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jelly2m8:<BR><B>  They just have to make the effort.<P>...hope this helps,...<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Great post.  Thanks!<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1578096&a=12001112&p=56509969&Sequence=0"> ||||reg||7
Z||000012||Rodney||12-06-2001||12:27 PM||||I have reproduced both coolant stickers. I also have the yellow fan starts stickers and the unleaded fuel stickers for the gas fill doors. Doing the emmissions info ones is much tougher. Possibly down the road some. ||||reg||1
